This directory holds the built web/ output (npm run build in web/, copied
here as `web/dist/* -> internal/coordinator/webassets/dist/`) so
webassets.go can go:embed it into the coordinator binary. It is
intentionally checked into git as an empty placeholder (this file) so
`go build ./...` keeps working with no frontend build present; deploy/Dockerfile's
node stage overwrites this directory's contents before the Go build stage
runs. Run `(cd web && npm ci && npm run build) && cp -r web/dist/. internal/coordinator/webassets/dist/`
locally to populate it for a non-Docker build.
